# Root .gitignore for the Olivares AI monorepo.
#
# Deliberately NARROW. Notable things that ARE tracked and must NOT be ignored:
#   - core/internal/webui/dist/**        (the embedded web bundle, go:embed)
#   - **/testdata/*.log                  (audit-connector fixtures — never add `*.log`)

# Local dependency trees, installed by `task setup`. The root package.json is
# commit-message tooling only (commitlint); the engine is Go, the web app is /web.
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH, on purpose (2026-08-05). A pattern ending in `/` matches only
# a DIRECTORY, so `web/node_modules` created as a SYMLINK — which is what pointing
# at a shared pnpm store produces, and what several of this repo's worktrees have —
# was NOT ignored and showed up as untracked. A `git add -A` would then commit a
# symlink to an absolute path outside the repository: broken for every other clone,
# and a path that escapes the tree in something we export publicly. Measured here,
# same class as the credential-shaped rules added in #537.
/node_modules
/web/node_modules
/clients/typescript/node_modules
# TypeScript client SDK build output (`pnpm --dir clients/typescript build`).
/clients/typescript/dist/
# Python bytecode + packaging caches (the Python client SDK; regenerated on
# import/test/build) and the generator's `go build` binary.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
/clients/generator/generator
# buf's temporary clone for `task proto:breaking` (kept off the small /tmp).
/.buftmp/
# examples/ smoke-test scratch (data dirs + extracted source-plugin binaries).
# On the workspace disk because /tmp is tmpfs+noexec in the dev container and the
# engine fork/execs the embedded connector plugin from $TMPDIR.
/.examples-tmp/
# The engine's LEGACY relative data directory. Until `olivares serve` with no
# --data-dir created this in whatever directory it was run from, so running the
# product from a clone dropped an installation into the tree. The default now
# resolves to a per-user path (cmd/olivares/boot.go defaultDataDir) and every data
# directory the engine creates carries its own exclusion (core/secure EnsureDataDir),
# so this line is the third layer, not the fix.
#
# It is NOT redundant with the `*.key`/`*.pem` rules at the end of this file, and
# that was measured on 2026-08-08 rather than assumed: those rules did catch the
# seven 0600 key files, but `git add -A` still staged olivares-data/olivares.db —
# the store, which holds the sealed secrets and the audit ledger — together with
# olivares-data/setup.token, the one-time token that creates the first administrator.
olivares-data/
# schema-parity gate's repo-local build scratch (two probe binaries; /tmp is
# noexec in the dev container so the gate builds under the worktree). Normally
# trap-removed, but gitignored so a SIGKILL/teardown leftover can't slip into git.
/.schema-parity.*/
# mapper-parity gate scratch (`task lint:error-mappers`): builds its AST helper, and its
# self-test writes throwaway module trees. /tmp is noexec in the dev container, so a gate
# that built there would refuse on every push of every lane unless the caller happened to
# have TMPDIR set — measured: exit 126, "permission denied" on a file whose exec bit is on.
# Trap-removed, but gitignored so a teardown leftover cannot slip into a commit.
/.error-mappers-tmp/
# truncated-list gate scratch (`task lint:list-page-discarded`): builds its AST helper,
# and /tmp is noexec in the dev container so the binary cannot live there. Trap-cleaned.
/.list-page-discarded-tmp/
/.cli-walk-tmp/

# openapi-op-descriptions gate's repo-local scratch. That gate COMPILES a binary and RUNS it, so
# it needs a scratch that is writable AND executable; /tmp is tmpfs+noexec in the dev container.
# The script CHOOSES its scratch (TMPDIR, then this, then /var/tmp) rather than having the task
# impose one — imposing it rejects on a read-only CI checkout and annuls a good TMPDIR the runner
# may supply. This entry exists because the fallback creates the parent, and an untracked
# directory in a SHARED clone is what a stray `git add -A` from another lane sweeps up.
/.openapi-op-tmp/

# config-env-docs gate's repo-local build scratch: it builds a Go helper and EXECUTES it,
# and its self-test writes throwaway repository trees. /tmp is noexec in the dev container,
# so the build lands here (same reason as .error-mappers-tmp/ above). Trap-cleaned.
/.config-env-docs-tmp/

#C09-03: the generated CLI-reference gate builds a Go helper, runs a command-tree
# walk and executes both. /tmp is noexec in the dev container, so the build lands here
# (same reason as .config-env-docs-tmp/ above). Trap-cleaned.
/.cli-ref-docs-tmp/

#C09-05: the guide gate (console reference, gRPC reference, upgrade-guide claims)
# builds a Go helper and EXECUTES it, and its self-test writes throwaway repository trees.
# /tmp is noexec in the dev container, so the build lands here (same reason as
# .config-env-docs-tmp/ above). Trap-cleaned.
/.guide-docs-tmp/

#C09-04: the published-OpenAPI-description gate builds a Go helper and EXECUTES it,
# and its self-test writes throwaway repository trees. /tmp is noexec in the dev container,
# so the build lands here (same reason as .config-env-docs-tmp/ above). Trap-cleaned.
/.openapi-op-descriptions-tmp/
# public-export gate scratch (`task lint:export`): builds the export-scrub helper and
# writes a throwaway curated copy; /tmp is noexec in the dev container so it runs under
# the worktree. Trap-removed, but gitignored so a teardown leftover can't slip in.
/.export-tmp/

# Artefacts of `task console:walk`, which writes 51 files into the CURRENT DIRECTORY by default
# (scripts/console-walk.mjs:46). Measured 2026-08-08: after a walk from the shared hub clone they
# sat there untracked, where any other lane's `git add -A` would have committed them. In a clone
# three containers share, an untracked artefact is not private -- it is everyone's. Point
# OLIVARES_WALK_OUT elsewhere if you want them kept.
/console-walk-out/
# lint:commerce builds the canon linter here rather than `go run`-ing it (go run
# does not propagate exit codes); /tmp is noexec in the dev container.
/.commerce-tmp/
# scripts/test-prepush-refclass.sh runs the real pre-push hook against STUB `task`/`git`
# executables, and PATH lookup needs the exec bit: /tmp is noexec in the dev container, so
# the battery falls back here. Trap-removed, but gitignored so a teardown leftover cannot
# slip into the index.
/.prepush-refclass-tmp/

# Local build outputs (the binary + release dir). The in-package form covers a
# `go build` run from cmd/olivares itself (a 60MB artifact once slipped into
# the index that way).
/olivares
/cmd/olivares/olivares
/dist/
/bin/
# First-party connector plugin binaries: BUILD ARTIFACTS, populated by
# `task build:connectors` (release) — only the embed-pattern placeholder is
# committed (the embed.go contract): ~249MB of blobs stay out of the index.
/cmd/olivares/firstparty/bins/*
!/cmd/olivares/firstparty/bins/PLACEHOLDER
# goreleaser-build-wrapper.sh's flock file (serializes per-target connector-embed
# builds) and release-smoke.sh's repo-local scratch (/tmp is tmpfs+noexec in the
# dev container, same reason as .examples-tmp/). Both are trap-/exit-cleaned;
# gitignored so a teardown leftover can't slip in.
/.connector-embed.lock
/.release-smoke-tmp/
# Astro/Starlight docs build output — regenerated by `astro build`, not committed.
/docs-site/dist/
/docs-site/node_modules/
# Astro's generated content cache — build artifact, regenerated on every build.
/docs-site/.astro/

# Java client SDK (clients/java) Maven build output — regenerated by `mvn` /
# `task sdk:test:java`, never committed (the generated source IS committed).
/clients/java/target/

# Commercial license Worker (commercial/license-worker): local deps, wrangler
# state, build output, and LOCAL SECRETS. .dev.vars holds the dev signing key + Polar/
# Resend secrets and must NEVER be committed (the .example template IS committed).
/commercial/license-worker/node_modules/
/commercial/license-worker/.wrangler/
/commercial/license-worker/dist/
/commercial/license-worker/.dev.vars

# OS / editor cruft.
.DS_Store

# Playwright run artifacts (web e2e + docs captures) — regenerated per run,
# never committed; the curated docs captures live in docs-site/src/assets/console/.
/web/playwright-report/
/web/test-results/

# commerce-lint build output (commercial/commerce-lint is its own Go module)
/commercial/commerce-lint/olivares-commerce-lint
.codex-briefs/

# exec-probe fallback tempdirs for the gate batteries when ${TMPDIR:-/tmp} is a
# noexec mount (see scripts/test-assert-cosign-binary.sh) — transient, trap-removed
/.tmpexec.*
.codex-input/

# ── CREDENTIAL-SHAPED FILES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Added 2026-08-05 after an audit for the public release found NO containment at all: the
# only rule of this family was one exact filename, and `git check-ignore` confirmed that
# .env, *.pem, *.key, *.p12, *.tfstate, id_rsa, id_ed25519 and .netrc would all have been
# staged by the next `git add -A`. Nothing bad was in the tree — the point is that nothing
# stood between the tree and the first mistake, and this repository is exported to a PUBLIC
# repository where a published credential cannot be taken back.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!*.env.example
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
id_ecdsa
id_ecdsa.*
.netrc
.npmrc
# Tracked and legitimate: a CA CERTIFICATE (no private key) used by the mcpb connector's
# trust-chain fixtures. Verified with `git ls-files '*.pem'` — it is the only one.
!connectors/mcpb/testdata/root.pem

# Playwright MCP scratch output (console logs + a11y snapshots from a driven browser).
# two of these were swept into a commit by `git add -A` during a real-run check.
# Verified secret-free before deciding not to rewrite history, but the tool writes them
# into the repo root on every run, so the fix is to stop them being trackable at all.
.playwright-mcp/

# ⛔ Estado local de wrangler. NO es higiene: `.wrangler/cache/wrangler-account.json` guarda el ID y
# el NOMBRE de la cuenta de Cloudflare, y este árbol se exporta a repositorios PÚBLICOS. Lo creó una
# consulta a D1 del criterio C-10 el 2026-08-17 y **un `git add -A` mío lo dejó en el índice**; lo
# cazó el gate de exportación al no poder clasificar la ruta —«nothing leaks by default»—, no un
# repaso a ojo. Medido antes de sacarlo: no contiene ningún correo, pero sí el id de 32 hex y el
# nombre. En un clon COMPARTIDO, además, lo que no está ignorado es de todos: el `git add -A` del
# siguiente carril se lo habría llevado igual.
.wrangler/

# El binario que deja un `go build`/`go test` DENTRO de scripts/guide-docs/. El gate no lo produce
# —compila a un scratch (`BIN="$SCRATCH/guide-docs"`, check-guide-docs.sh:73)— pero desde que ese
# paquete tiene tests, correrlos a mano deja 4,2 MB sin trackear en el arbol. Y un artefacto de
# compilacion sin trackear no es solo desorden: el 2026-08-21, 117 MB de residuo de `lint:export`
# en `.export-tmp/` hicieron que `lint:guide-docs` acusara al arbol por copias de si mismo.
/scripts/guide-docs/guide-docs
/.overlay-fetch-seal

# ⛔ RESIDUO DE `tofu init`, Y NO ES HIGIENE: ENVENENA UN GATE 485 LINTS DESPUÉS.
#
# Medido el 2026-08-29. Corrí `tofu init` dentro de `deploy/aws` para poder producir un plan
# en frío, y dejó `.terraform.lock.hcl` en el árbol. `lint:spdx` lo encontró **sin trackear
# y sin ignorar**, no supo clasificar la extensión `.hcl` y —correctamente— contestó
# **«CANNOT LOOK», rc=2**: no es una violación de licencia y NO es un aprobado, es que el
# gate no sabe si eso es fuente. Tumbó el push en el lint 485 de 648.
#
# El fallo no fue del gate: fue mío por correr una herramienta dentro del árbol de trabajo.
# Estas reglas hacen que el descuido no vuelva a costar una corrida.
#
# ⚠ DECISIÓN PENDIENTE, dicha aquí para que no se pierda: un `.terraform.lock.hcl`
# COMMITEADO es buena práctica —fija las versiones de proveedor y hace el apply
# reproducible—, y hoy este repositorio no tiene ninguno. Ignorarlo es lo correcto para un
# artefacto accidental como el que provocó esto, pero NO cierra esa pregunta: adoptarlo a
# propósito exigiría además darle una regla a `.hcl` en `classify()` de `check-spdx.sh`.
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
*.tfplan
anchoridt.*
